# Line endings. Only the files that Docker, a Linux shell or the CI runner executes are forced to LF: a CRLF in a
# Dockerfile, a shell script or a workflow can break the build or the script on Linux (for example a carriage return
# glued to a command or to a path). Nothing else is normalised here, so the rest of the repository keeps its current
# endings and no history is rewritten; widen this file deliberately, in its own change, if that is ever wanted.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
deploy/** text eol=lf
.github/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/*.py text eol=lf
